  "content": {
    "text": "Space Watch\nSpaceX already needs to raise more cash, and its stock is falling 10%\nElon Musk’s company is turning to the bond market less than two weeks after its blockbuster IPO\nFresh off its historic initial public offering, SpaceX needs to raise even more cash — this time through the debt market.\nThe company said in a Monday filing that it planned to offer senior unsecured notes to “qualified institutional investors.” Last week, Moody’s Ratings, Fitch Ratings and S&P Global Ratings awarded SpaceX investment-grade bond ratings.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "Space Watch",
      "SpaceX already needs to raise more cash, and its stock is falling 10%",
      "Elon Musk’s company is turning to the bond market less than two weeks after its blockbuster IPO",
      "Fresh off its historic initial public offering, SpaceX needs to raise even more cash — this time through the debt market.",
      "The company said in a Monday filing that it planned to offer senior unsecured notes to “qualified institutional investors.” Last week, Moody’s Ratings, Fitch Ratings and S&P Global Ratings awarded SpaceX investment-grade bond ratings."
